<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RMP mulls restructuring.</title>
<headline>RMP mulls restructuring.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>RMP Properties Ltd said it was considering rationalising the listing of RMP and Barprop Ltd with the possibility of listing the land clearing and gold recovery operations seperately.</p>
<p>The capital of RMP would also be restructured into linked units, the company said.</p>
<p>The rationale for the rationalisation was to optimise RMP's assets and improve tradeability on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>A further announcement would be made within the next six weeks, the company said. Shareholders were urged to exercise caution in their share dealings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
